## How to log it (paper, isolated — never touches live model)

New strategy tag: `V529_PAPER_BASKET_YES`

Store as its OWN paper bets so it can be filtered clean, exactly like the
existing paper tags. Do NOT mix into single-bracket P&L.

Suggested per-basket record (in bets table, or a small companion table):
- date, city
- bracket_A_label, price_A
- bracket_B_label, price_B
- combined_cost = price_A + price_B
- model_prob_A, model_prob_B, combined_model_prob
- placed_at (need the time-of-day; basket is afternoon-only)
- result: which bracket settled (A / B / neither)
- profit = (1.00 − combined_cost − fees) if A or B hit, else −(combined_cost+fees)
- strategy_tag = 'V529_PAPER_BASKET_YES'

Fees: model Kalshi's actual per-contract fee for 2 contracts so paper P&L is
honest. Do not log fee-free profit — the whole point is the fee is what makes
or breaks this.

---

## What success looks like (the test)

After enough settled paper baskets (target 50+, same discipline as everything):

Compare `V529_PAPER_BASKET_YES` ROI against:
- single-bracket bets in the SAME 45-69¢ middle zone (which lost money in July)
- doing nothing (skip)

Basket EARNS its place ONLY if its ROI, AFTER modeled fees, beats both. If the
combined cost consistently eats the edge (fees + prices too high), the idea is
dead and you stop wondering — same bar as the ECMWF shadow test.

---

## What NOT to do

- Do NOT build this during the highs validation window.
- Do NOT bet real money on it before 50+ settled paper baskets.
- Do NOT basket in the morning (fees + loose prices = negative EV).
- Do NOT basket when combined cost ≥ ~0.95 (no room after fees).
- Do NOT treat "high win rate" as success — a basket that wins 95% of the time
  but pays 8¢ per win after fees can still be net-negative. ROI after fees is
  the only measure that matters.

